# AI-Enabled Skill Intelligence & Learning Platform (Prototype)

**Organization:** MoSPI — Data Informatics & Innovation Division (DIID)
**Theme:** Smart Education — Capacity building for India's Official Statistical System

A working prototype of the platform described in the problem statement:
- AI-based competency assessment & automated skill-gap analysis
- Personalized learning recommendations (mock iGOT Karmayogi + NSSTA TPAC course catalog)
- AI-powered MCQ / quiz generation from uploaded learning material (.txt / .pdf / .docx)
- Employee dashboard (competency radar, gaps, recommendations, enrollments)
- Admin dashboard (org-wide readiness, top skill gaps, training effectiveness)
- Admin user management — add, edit, and delete officials/admin accounts
  (Admin Analytics → Manage Users)

## Tech stack
- Backend: Python 3.10+, Flask, Flask-SQLAlchemy (SQLite)
- Recommendation engine: scikit-learn (TF-IDF + cosine similarity)
- MCQ generation: built-in offline rule-based NLP engine, with optional
  upgrade to Anthropic Claude for higher-quality LLM-generated questions
- Frontend: Server-rendered Jinja2 templates, Bootstrap 5, Chart.js (no build step)

## Setup (VS Code / local)

```bash
# 1. Create and activate a virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# 2. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. (Optional) enable LLM-based quiz generation
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...      # Windows (PowerShell): $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# 4. Run the app
python app.py
```

Open **http://localhost:5000** in your browser. The database (SQLite) and five
demo users (four officials + one admin) are auto-created on first run — no
extra setup needed. Click any user on the landing page to "log in" (this is a
prototype auth-lite switcher; swap in SSO/RBAC for production per the DIID spec).

