## How each requirement maps to the code

| Problem statement requirement | Where it's implemented |
|---|---|
| Competency profile from designation/role/experience | `modules/models.py` (`User`, `Competency`), `templates/profile.html` |
| Skill-gap analysis vs framework | `modules/competency_engine.py` |
| 4 competency domains (Statistical/Technical/Digital Gov/Behavioural) | `data/competency_framework.json`, `DOMAIN_MAP` |
| iGOT Karmayogi + NSSTA TPAC integration | `data/igot_courses.json` (mock catalog — replace with live API calls), `modules/recommender.py` |
| Personalized learning pathways | `recommend_courses()` in `modules/recommender.py` |
| AI-powered MCQ/quiz generation from uploaded material | `modules/quiz_generator.py`, routes `/quiz/generate`, `/quiz/<id>` |
| Instant evaluation + explanations | `/quiz/<id>/submit` route, `templates/quiz_result.html` |
| Employee dashboard | `templates/employee_dashboard.html` |
| Admin dashboard (org-wide analytics, predictive needs) | `templates/admin_dashboard.html` |
| Secure, scalable web platform | Flask + SQLAlchemy ORM (swap SQLite → PostgreSQL for production), role-based routes (`is_admin`) |

## Extending this prototype toward production

- **Real iGOT Karmayogi integration:** replace `modules/recommender.py`'s
  `load_courses()` with live calls to the iGOT Karmayogi course-catalog and
  enrollment APIs (the mock JSON mirrors the shape you'd get back).
- **LLM quiz generation:** already wired via `modules/quiz_generator.py` —
  just set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. Swap the `model` parameter or provider as needed.
- **Auth:** replace the demo user-switcher (`/login/<id>`) with SSO
  (e.g. SAML/OIDC against the government identity provider) and proper RBAC.
- **Scale:** move from SQLite to PostgreSQL, containerize with Docker, and
  put the app behind Gunicorn/Nginx for production deployment.
